PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1773658155
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G15/28
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The prime minister of the Republic of
OL,6, Ireland has asked the United States for
OL,7, support for the Anglo-Irish agreement.
OL,9,FDr Garret FitzGerald, on a week's visit
OL,10,Fto the US, said the British and Irish
OL,11,Fgovernments would implement the deal -
OL,12,Fregardless of Unionist intimidation.
OL,14,FHe also urged US supporters of Irish
OL,15,Fnationalism to try to understand why
OL,16,FUnionists felt betrayed.
OL,18,FDr FitzGerald was speaking at Dickson
OL,19,FCity, Pennsylvania, to mark the St
OL,20,FPatrick's Day celebrations in the US.
OL,23,T]CFrom 16-03-86 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
